      "value": "@{62238ce4213aae67e9773fad|full_name} I might know how to fix it, so launch vrchat in auto rotate mode, then once in a world, rotate back to landscape and lock your screen rotation then rotate the phone upside down with selfie expression mode on with your camera facing you., then cover the camera after so your head will stay facing upright and do not get in the cameras view at all after this, then turn selfy expression off comepletely. its because camera tracking is a core part of the apps code and it doesnt matter the avi because it is using your phones camera and due to androids permissions I believe the camera on your phone comepletely ignores the avis last use states.",
